Off, leaving Bishkek, going to Almaty

00:00:19.624 --> 00:00:22.791
and here is the process.

00:00:23.538 --> 00:00:26.041
I'm in a taxi now
but we're going to another taxi

00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:29.589
and you get a shared car,
basically, with a driver.

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:33.038
Once it fills up with people, you leave.

00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:35.492
-Da? (Yes)
-Da.

00:00:35.492 --> 00:00:36.456
-Okay.

00:00:36.456 --> 00:00:37.450
And she's helping me.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:42.641
She's helped me
find the right guy and negotiate

00:00:42.641 --> 00:00:48.965
because if you don't know the prices,
you most likely....

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.204
Most likely get screwed.

00:00:51.204 --> 00:00:54.104
So I asked her to do
some negotiation for me.

00:00:55.099 --> 00:00:56.099
[Russian]

00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:06.081
They're connected like aspen trees.

00:01:06.081 --> 00:01:07.723
Everybody knows everybody.

00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:10.781
Sometimes there's infighting,
sometimes they help each other out.

00:01:10.781 --> 00:01:12.357
So that was pretty easy.

00:01:12.357 --> 00:01:13.654
He said go to this guy.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:19.734
[Russian]

00:01:26.779 --> 00:01:31.771
Nobody's on this ride and I gotta get
to the airport in Almaty at...

00:01:31.771 --> 00:01:33.451
I gotta be there by 5:30.

00:01:33.857 --> 00:01:37.482
So if we do leave in two hours
like he said is possible

00:01:37.482 --> 00:01:40.635
that's no-go,
that's a missed flight situation.

00:01:40.686 --> 00:01:44.737
I thought there would be
many, many people but...

00:01:47.646 --> 00:01:48.686
There aren't.

00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:51.684
So we gotta fill this thing up.

00:01:51.684 --> 00:01:54.759
We gotta fill the van up and then we go.

00:01:58.695 --> 00:01:59.695
[Russian]

00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:07.925
[Russian]

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.806
-Thank you.

00:02:30.085 --> 00:02:31.085
[Russian]

00:02:32.913 --> 00:02:33.913
-Almaty?

00:02:41.037 --> 00:02:42.717
Zamir, he's a class guy.

00:02:43.148 --> 00:02:44.720
-Good evening, good evening.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.920
Good afternoon.

00:02:47.149 --> 00:02:49.202
-Zamir was going for
the hard sale in the beginning

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.135
but then he really warmed up.

00:02:51.433 --> 00:02:53.008
I feel like we got a good driver.

00:02:53.563 --> 00:02:54.734
[Russian]

00:02:55.039 --> 00:02:57.074
Zamir just offered me a deal.

00:02:57.074 --> 00:03:03.316
He said he'll drive me alone
to the airport in Almaty for $65.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.851
It's roughly five hours, the drive

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:09.156
and I love the experiences
of filling the car up

00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:12.424
and connecting with random people

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:17.838
but I definitely messed this situation up
and came too late this morning.

00:03:17.838 --> 00:03:21.524
So don't do that
if you're going Bishkek to Almaty.

00:03:22.058 --> 00:03:25.194
From what he's saying,
do it early in the morning.

00:03:25.435 --> 00:03:27.368
I'm gonna take Zamir's offer.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.156
-Zamir...
-Zamir. [chuckles]

00:03:30.156 --> 00:03:32.090
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:03:32.216 --> 00:03:36.120
-He's pumped, he doesn't have to wait
and he gets the full price.

00:03:36.677 --> 00:03:38.911
Yeah, off to the border.

00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:41.005
-[chuckling] Okay.

00:03:41.885 --> 00:03:47.882
-Just for the record, the Kyrgys do
drive a little mad I will say.

00:03:48.155 --> 00:03:51.273
It feels very peaceful on the streets

00:03:51.273 --> 00:03:53.871
but I feel like
all the aggression is let out

00:03:53.871 --> 00:03:56.356
behind the steering wheel
and the gas pedal.

00:03:56.829 --> 00:04:00.537
Zamir's trying to
poke through this intersection.

00:04:01.918 --> 00:04:02.918
[honking]

00:04:03.369 --> 00:04:04.369
Nice, Zamir.

00:04:04.665 --> 00:04:05.665
[Russian]

00:04:10.061 --> 00:04:14.080
Getting close to the Kazakh border
and I made the fatal mistake

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.345
of giving money first.

00:04:17.345 --> 00:04:21.432
He wanted it all and I gave him half.

00:04:22.218 --> 00:04:25.153
So I got a weird feeling right now
there's a bit of a scam going on.

00:04:25.153 --> 00:04:28.887
As in I don't see him
on the other side of the border

00:04:28.887 --> 00:04:33.303
'cause I gotta go through customs,
he's gotta go through with his car.

00:04:33.483 --> 00:04:34.995
So this should be interesting.

00:04:34.995 --> 00:04:37.929
I got a weird feeling.

00:04:37.929 --> 00:04:40.562
Normally always give money
at the end with a taxi driver.

00:04:40.562 --> 00:04:41.981
It's like I always do that

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:45.471
and since we don't have
anyone in the vehicle, I thought,

00:04:45.471 --> 00:04:49.869
"Well, he needs some gas money,
I'll give him half up front."

00:04:49.869 --> 00:04:51.932
I wasn't really on my A game.

00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:56.958
So we'll see if I see
Zamir on the other side.

00:04:59.277 --> 00:05:03.173
Right beyond that flag is Kazakhstan.

00:05:35.085 --> 00:05:36.598
I got that totally wrong.

00:05:36.598 --> 00:05:37.598
I thought...

00:05:39.146 --> 00:05:41.476
I thought he was scamming me and he's not.

00:05:41.476 --> 00:05:43.499
It's really cool
but I've heard of a lot of people

00:05:43.499 --> 00:05:45.565
getting scammed at this border.

00:05:45.648 --> 00:05:48.576
And so I do have a history here.

00:05:48.576 --> 00:05:51.986
I have a very interesting history.

00:05:52.154 --> 00:05:53.154
[Russian]

00:05:55.684 --> 00:05:56.684
-Okay.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:06:00.309
-Sixteen years ago
I was traveling with a friend of mine.

00:06:02.469 --> 00:06:05.282
I was traveling with a friend of mine

00:06:05.282 --> 00:06:08.531
and we got to the other side

00:06:08.531 --> 00:06:10.731
and I lost him, his name's Gavin.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.345
And we were with a shared taxi,
many people in it

00:06:15.345 --> 00:06:16.962
and we didn't know where he went.

00:06:16.962 --> 00:06:19.719
We waited for like an hour
and so this one lady,

00:06:19.719 --> 00:06:26.986
this very tough, authoritative-type woman
went looking for him.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:30.927
Well, we all went looking for him
but then she found him in a car.

00:06:30.927 --> 00:06:35.802
In the back of a car
with this smoking hot woman.

00:06:36.502 --> 00:06:40.961
"It was like a super model." he said,
and two militzia, two policemen.

00:06:41.527 --> 00:06:44.599
And they were trying to
extract money out of him.

00:06:44.822 --> 00:06:46.754
So they wouldn't let him leave the car

00:06:46.778 --> 00:06:48.566
but he said it was
this interesting situation

00:06:48.566 --> 00:06:52.735
where he was in the back of car
with a smoking hot woman

00:06:52.735 --> 00:06:56.138
and, you know,
they're just sort of hanging out.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:58.431
So that was 16 years ago here.

00:06:58.431 --> 00:07:00.998
I think things have cleaned up quite a bit.

00:07:00.998 --> 00:07:05.543
From my experiences so far
in these two countries, this trip

00:07:05.543 --> 00:07:07.625
it's way easier to get around.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:16.439
Okay... [Russian] It's all good?

00:07:16.439 --> 00:07:17.439
-Yeah.

00:07:18.867 --> 00:07:21.019
-That's how you say your name, Sheshwan?

00:07:21.019 --> 00:07:22.834
-Jazwan.
-Jazwan?

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:24.855
-Just call me Jess.
-Jazwan.

00:07:25.516 --> 00:07:28.064
A very friendly border agent, Jazwan.

00:07:28.131 --> 00:07:31.890
16 years ago I came through here
and it was totally different.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.890
[chuckles]

00:07:33.445 --> 00:07:35.671
-This is real progress, haha.

00:07:35.671 --> 00:07:37.201
-Seriously, bro.
-Yeah.

00:07:37.201 --> 00:07:40.101
-My friend was, like,
held hostage over there.

00:07:40.825 --> 00:07:44.649
Seriously, two militzia guys
put him in the back of the car,

00:07:44.649 --> 00:07:49.127
wanted money and they had, like,
a super model back there in the car too.

00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:53.047
[hands slap]

00:07:53.047 --> 00:07:54.396
-Have a nice trip.
-All right, bro.

00:07:54.396 --> 00:07:58.182
Kazakhstan is definitely
much different this time coming in.

00:07:58.182 --> 00:07:59.382
Take care, bro.

00:07:59.639 --> 00:08:02.801
Very cool, I mean I've never been
to a border where they've said,

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:06.321
"Yeah, put your camera up
and take footage if you want."

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:12.049
It's so cool to see
the changes in the world.

00:08:12.049 --> 00:08:13.950
Like, everything's always changing.

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.051
It's either getting better or worse.

00:08:16.051 --> 00:08:22.766
I would say this border into Kazakhstan,
in general, is on the much better trend.

00:08:23.487 --> 00:08:25.618
In as far as letting tourists in.

00:08:25.618 --> 00:08:28.218
Before, it was super hard to get visas.

00:08:28.218 --> 00:08:30.160
It was a pain in the ass.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.772
You needed to do all this documentation

00:08:31.772 --> 00:08:37.181
and now it's simple, no visa,
just write on a little piece of paper

00:08:37.181 --> 00:08:38.832
and go through in 10 minutes.

00:08:39.022 --> 00:08:40.686
There's Zamir. Zamir's calling me.

00:08:40.686 --> 00:08:41.686
Zamir...

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:43.840
[Russian]

00:08:44.268 --> 00:08:45.268
All is good.

