00:13:57.413 --> 00:14:02.371
What's very interesting
in this part of the world

00:14:02.371 --> 00:14:07.022
is the Soviet Union
comprised of 15 countries

00:14:07.022 --> 00:14:11.555
and there's some sameness about them

00:14:11.555 --> 00:14:15.523
but they also have
their own unique identities.

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:19.047
So the "stan" countries,
there's five of them

00:14:19.047 --> 00:14:23.854
and they’re all different
but there's some Russification feeling

00:14:23.854 --> 00:14:25.688
that you feel in all of them.

00:14:25.688 --> 00:14:29.141
And then you can go to Estonia
and that's a completely different world.

00:14:29.141 --> 00:14:30.615
It's much more European.

00:14:30.615 --> 00:14:31.514
[honking]

00:14:31.514 --> 00:14:35.338
So after traveling
in this part of the world long enough

00:14:35.338 --> 00:14:42.926
you come to realize it's crazy
it stayed together as long as it did.

00:14:42.926 --> 00:14:48.518
Because it has so many cultures,
such expansive territory,

00:14:48.518 --> 00:14:49.857
so many languages.

00:14:49.857 --> 00:14:55.362
So many different languages
were in the former Soviet Union.

00:14:55.362 --> 00:14:56.903
Are in the former Soviet Union.

00:14:56.903 --> 00:14:57.903
So...

00:14:59.866 --> 00:15:02.661
What did it last, 70-ish odd years?

00:15:04.489 --> 00:15:05.932
I don't know how it kept together.

00:15:05.932 --> 00:15:09.829
because Kazakhstan and Kyrgyzstan
have a lot of similarities.

00:15:09.829 --> 00:15:15.839
They're different, but then you take
Kazakhstan and Estonia or Georgia

00:15:15.839 --> 00:15:19.282
and those are different worlds completely.

00:15:19.691 --> 00:15:20.778
Uh...

00:15:20.778 --> 00:15:23.463
No, no, no... Nyet, nyet, nyet...

00:15:23.463 --> 00:15:24.463
[Russian]

00:15:27.306 --> 00:15:29.306
Yeah, it's really fascinating.

00:15:30.561 --> 00:15:32.825
This part of the world is often overlooked

00:15:32.825 --> 00:15:38.557
and for me, it's one of my favorites,
if not my favorite.

00:15:38.557 --> 00:15:44.047
Because it's not at all
what we were taught, for sure.

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:46.833
Like, we were taught Moscow.

00:15:46.833 --> 00:15:51.972
The look was gray apartment buildings
and skies in Moscow.

00:15:51.972 --> 00:15:58.114
It wasn't massive mountains
and different cultures, that's for sure.

00:16:02.614 --> 00:16:08.403
